{
 "_doc": "Belt item sounds (BeltSfx, docs/AUDIO.md), keyed by belt item id (content/utility). Every item has start (the use cue, played at the Hunter when it is used) and end. Channels (tonic, armor_kit and the drinks): loop held while it channels, end when it finishes, cancel when it is spilt (hit, stunned, rolled). \"beds\": where the item's run is heard: a loop (if it has one) at the spot for the item's own time, then its end cue; \"front\" = ahead of the user by the item's \"range\" (1.6 m without one, a pad's spot), \"aim\" = where they aim, \"here\" = where they stand, \"self\" = following the user, \"buff\" = following the user with the loop quiet (BeltSfx.BUFF_DB), ended early when the buff is gone (a shield broken). An item's time is its \"time\" or \"life\", else its first effect's \"time\" or \"delay\" (Shatter's blast), else \"tails\": seconds from the use to the end cue of an instant item. A pad used once is cut to its \"after\", a pack picked up ends there. hit = a pad launched someone. Keys play theirs when they open a lock (BeltKeys). --sfx-set-check asserts every belt item has its own start and end, none a shared stock cue.",
